  "label": "The person in the image is mapped as 'my face' when waiting for cookies",
  "description": "The text 'my face when im wating' directly maps the visual entity 'clergy' (specifically, the central figure in the red chasuble, whose solemn expression is contrasted with the mundane context) to the textual concept of 'my face' — implying the viewer's own face in a state of impatience. The humor arises from the absurd juxtaposition: the solemn, reverent expression of the clergy is humorously equated with the viewer's face while impatiently waiting for cookies to bake. The mapping is established by the text overlay explicitly labeling the visual subject as 'my face'.",
